# Everything the API needs, and nothing it does not.
#
# `cp server/.env.example server/.env` and fill in the two keys. This file used
# to hold one line — and that line was a *frontend* variable pointing at a
# contract two deployments out of date — while the README told people to copy it
# and add RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY and COACH_ADDRESS, neither of which was in it. A
# judge following the quickstart could not start the server.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- required

# Pays the gas so that somebody who lifts weights does not need a coin. It signs
# nothing on anybody's behalf: the owner is a field inside the message the
# device signed, so the worst a compromised relayer can do is refuse to help.
# Fund it at https://faucet.0g.ai for Galileo.
RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Opens coaches, and pays for inference on 0G Compute.
#
# Devices seal a new coach to this key's *public* half, served at
# /api/coach/pubkey. Changing it makes every existing coach unopenable — there
# is no migration, because the blobs are anchored on chain by hash. Treat a
# rotation as a decision, not a config change.
#
# It may be the same key as the relayer; a separate one keeps the wallet that
# holds funds apart from the one that reads coaches.
COACH_SERVICE_KEY=

# The deployed CoachAgent. Without it the coach card stays hidden — a fork with
# no contract is not broken, it simply has no coach yet.
COACH_ADDRESS=0x0253fb92F9e88E82Fb0632C076C88204e4400025

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- optional

# 0G Galileo testnet by default. Set both together or every signature is for a
# chain nobody is on.
# OG_RPC_URL=https://evmrpc-testnet.0g.ai
# OG_CHAIN_ID=16602

# Comma-separated fallbacks, tried when the primary is unreachable. 0G's docs
# recommend a third-party RPC for production (QuickNode, ThirdWeb, Ankr, dRPC);
# they issue per-account endpoints, so there is nothing sensible to ship here.
# OG_RPC_FALLBACK_URLS=

# OG_INDEXER_URL=https://indexer-storage-testnet-turbo.0g.ai

# How long 0G Storage gets before a write or read is abandoned. The default is
# 60s: long enough for finality on a healthy network, short enough that a
# serverless function is not killed with nothing to report.
# OG_STORAGE_TIMEOUT_MS=60000

# Everything we will relay for everybody, per day. The per-address limit is
# keyed on an address the caller chooses, so this is the one that cannot be
# stepped around by inventing identities.
# MAX_RELAYS_PER_DAY=400

# Postgres, when this runs somewhere with no disk it can keep. Without it the
# server writes to DATA_DIR, which on a serverless platform is thrown away
# between requests — so every account created survives until the next request
# lands on a different instance.
# DATABASE_URL=

# DATA_DIR=./data

# Passkeys are bound to an origin: these must match where the app is served
# from, or sign-in stops working with no useful error.
# ORIGIN=http://localhost:8080
# RP_ID=localhost

# Shared secret for the scheduled reminder sweep, when a platform cron pokes it.
# CRON_SECRET=
